+### 3.8 Unified Cache External Linker (UMBP)
 
-UMBP is the second way to spill KV off the GPU, and it is an **alternative to [HiCache](#3-3-hicache-hierarchical-kv-caching), not a tier inside it**. HiCache is a hierarchy — GPU, then pinned host memory, then optionally a storage backend. UMBP links the unified radix tree straight to MORI's buffer pool with no host cache tier in between, so pages load and offload against the external store directly. SGLang rejects the two together, so enabling the **UMBP** card in the [Playground above](#playground) strips the whole HiCache flag family from the command:
+The **unified cache external linker** is the second way to move KV cache off the GPU. The linker is the SGLang feature, and you enable it with `--enable-unified-cache-external-linker`. UMBP is one store the linker can use; you select it with `--unified-cache-external-linker-backend mori`. The Playground card uses the feature name, not the store name.
+
+The linker is an **alternative to [HiCache](#3-3-hicache-hierarchical-kv-caching), not a tier inside it**. HiCache is a hierarchy — GPU, then pinned host memory, then optionally a storage backend. The linker connects the unified radix tree directly to the external store, with no host cache tier in between, so pages load and offload against that store. SGLang rejects the two together, so enabling the **Unified Cache External Linker** card in the [Playground above](#playground) strips the whole HiCache flag family from the command:
 
 ```bash Command
 --enable-unified-cache-external-linker \
 --unified-cache-external-linker-backend mori
 ```
 
