+### ConvRot INT8
+
+`convrot_int8` (formerly `kitchen_int8`, still accepted as a deprecated alias)
+is online W8A8 INT8 for DiTs and compatible native encoders:
+every linear whose input dim is divisible by the Hadamard group size (256) is
+rotated and quantized per output channel after loading a stock BF16 checkpoint
+(ConvRot, arXiv:2512.03673; no calibration data). Each forward call runs one
+fused op per linear: group-wise Hadamard rotation, dynamic per-row INT8
+activation quantization, INT8 GEMM, dequantization and bias add.
+
+Two kernel backends implement the same quantization and consume the same INT8
+weights and per-row scales, so the choice is made per layer at load time:
+
+- `jit`: the `convrot_int8` ops in `sglang.kernels.ops.gemm.convrot_int8`,
+  compiled by SGLang's JIT for the local GPU on first use (about a minute with
+  `nvcc` on the machine; cached under `SGLANG_JIT_CACHE_DIR`, default
+  `~/.cache/sglang/jit`, for later runs). CC 9.0 (Hopper), 10.0 (B200, GB200)
+  and 12.0 / 12.1 (RTX PRO 6000 Blackwell, RTX 50 series, DGX Spark); group
+  size 64, 128, 256 or 512; output width a multiple of 8. CC 10.3 (B300,
+  GB300) is refused on purpose: Blackwell Ultra cuts INT8 tensor-core
+  throughput to a fraction of its BF16 rate, so use FP8 or NVFP4 there. Linears sharing one input (a block's Q/K/V projections)
+  rotate and quantize it once, and the Qwen-Image FFN down-projection folds its
+  GELU(tanh) into the rotate kernel; both are bitwise identical to the
+  per-linear ops.
+- `comfy_kitchen`: `comfy_kitchen.int8_linear` from the optional
+  `comfy-kitchen` package (`pip install comfy-kitchen`). Turing and later
+  (SM75); group size 16, 64 or 256.
+
+The default `auto` takes `jit` wherever its ops build and run (no CUDA
+toolchain, or a failed build, counts as unavailable and is logged) and
+`comfy_kitchen` otherwise; loading stops with an install hint if
+`comfy-kitchen` is then missing. A layer whose output width is not a multiple
+of 8 goes to `comfy_kitchen` when it is installed and stays BF16 otherwise.
+`SGLANG_DIFFUSION_CONVROT_INT8_BACKEND=jit` or `=comfy_kitchen` forces one
+backend. LoRA adapters run in dynamic mode (they cannot be merged into
+rotated INT8 weights); under FSDP `auto` resolves to `comfy_kitchen` and an
+explicit `jit` is refused. Serialized Comfy ConvRot INT8 DiTs and native
+encoders use `--component-weights-paths.<component>`; they are auto-detected
+from per-layer markers, load INT8 weights and row scales directly (omit online
+quantization), and follow the same per-layer backend choice.
+`--transformer-weights-path` remains the primary-DiT convenience spelling.
 
