+## Image inputs
+
+Both `/v1/decisions` and `/v1/systemone` accept an optional top-level `images` list. Each item uses the same image URL object as `image_url` in [vision chat requests](/docs/basic_usage/openai_api_vision), with `url` and optional `detail`, or is a string holding the `url` alone, such as a data URL or base64 image bytes. Use a vision-capable generation model with its vision encoder loaded and a Jinja template that accepts image parts. Some vision models serve text only unless the server is launched with `--enable-multimodal`. The native processor must expose image marker metadata, and a custom chat template is refused if it fails to preserve one complete marker per image. The server uses SGLang's existing image processor and vision encoder, placing the images in list order before the existing text in every question's user message.
+
+Save an image as `screenshot.png` and send it to the server launched above:
+
+```python Example
+import base64
+from pathlib import Path
+
+import requests
+
+response = requests.post(
+    "http://127.0.0.1:30000/v1/decisions",
+    json={
+        "input": "Use the screenshot to answer the question.",
+        "images": [{"url": base64.b64encode(Path("screenshot.png").read_bytes()).decode("ascii")}],
+        "questions": [{"id": "menu", "type": "yes_no", "question": "A menu is visible."}],
+    },
+    timeout=60,
+)
+response.raise_for_status()
+print(response.json()["answers"]["menu"])
+```
+
+You can also supply an image URL. On `/v1/systemone`, send the same `images` field over HTTP alongside `state` and its question map. Images are shared by all questions. Objects and arrays in `input` or `state` remain JSON text, and text-only prompt wording stays at version 1. Image requests are refused when `--allow-auto-truncate` is enabled because truncation could remove the answer position. `return_prompt_token_ids` is unsupported with images because token IDs alone cannot replay vision conditioning through `/v1/score`.
+
+Image requests are also refused when `input`, `state` or a question contains the model's own image, video or audio marker text, because the processor would read that text as media. Each question of an image request is prepared and scheduled on its own, so a probability near a tie can differ slightly between identical requests. Launch the server with `--enable-deterministic-inference` when image answers must repeat exactly, as described in [deterministic inference](/docs/advanced_features/deterministic_inference).
+
