From 3bb8cc1dc2425cde5fb6ab1c4a77edfab8c19715 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: wangyuzhan <wangyuzhan@bytedance.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 14:26:44 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] test(dsv4): drop the mocked full-topk decode runtime test

Review flagged test_full_topk_decode_runtime_integration with the same
rationale as the CPU wiring tests: it hand-assembles FullTopKIndexer via
object.__new__ and stubs decode_scores, so beyond the direct kernel tests
it only pins the _torch_decode call site's argument plumbing -- and with
bs == rows even the [:bs] slices it purports to check are no-ops. The
kernel's behavior stays covered by test_page_transform_matches_reference
and the other topk tests here, which call the real kernel directly.

